import Foundation

// The interaction token of the input event being handled (roadmap/16 §14.1).
//
// The platform sets the token around each key press and pointer button press
// it hands an application, and clears it when the event is handled. An
// application reads it while it handles that event, to ask for something the
// person just did: a paste, a grant, a picker. Outside an event there is none.
//
// A token is not a permission by being read. The Presence service verifies it
// with MosaicDisplay before it acts (§14), and an id that was not minted for
// a hardware event fails that check.

// Sets the token of the event now being handled, or clears it with none. Only
// the platform calls this; an application that calls it gains nothing, since
// its token must still verify.
public function interactionDispatch(token: InteractionToken?) {
    library.interaction = token
}

// The token of the event now being handled, or none outside an event.
public function interactionCurrent() -> InteractionToken? {
    return library.interaction
}
